# Suppliers through the gateway, in the order a reader would try them. Start the stack with
# `docker compose up -d`, then run the requests top to bottom: sam (supplier-admin) creates, proposes and
# submits; sofia (supplier-approver) checks the account, approves it and activates the supplier.

@gateway = http://localhost:5300/api

### Log in as sam, supplier-admin.
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/matchbook/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=sam&password=matchbook

### Log in as sofia, supplier-approver.
# @name approverLogin
POST http://localhost:8080/realms/matchbook/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=matchbook-cli&username=sofia&password=matchbook

### Create a supplier as a draft (add "id": "<a GUID>" to make a retry return the same supplier).
# @name create
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Acme GmbH",
  "taxId": "DE {{$randomInt 100000000 999999999}}",
  "countryCode": "DE",
  "paymentTermsDays": 30,
  "contactEmail": "ap@acme.example"
}

### Read it back; any supplier role or the auditor may.
GET {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Correct the details; a changed name, country or terms is published once the supplier is active.
PUT {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Acme Deutschland GmbH",
  "taxId": "{{create.response.body.taxId}}",
  "countryCode": "DE",
  "paymentTermsDays": 45,
  "contactEmail": "ap@acme.example"
}

### Propose a bank account; sam's own response shows the IBAN masked.
# @name propose
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/bank-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "iban": "DE89 3704 0044 0532 0130 00",
  "bic": "DEUTDEFF",
  "accountHolder": "Acme Deutschland GmbH"
}

### Try to approve it as sam: 403 supplier.role_required, a second person has to.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/bank-accounts/{{propose.response.body.bankAccounts[0].id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Sofia reviews the supplier and sees the pending IBAN in full, to check it against the supplier's letter.
GET {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Sofia approves the account; it is now in force with account version 1.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/bank-accounts/{{propose.response.body.bankAccounts[0].id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Sam submits the draft for activation.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}

### Sofia sees what is waiting for her: suppliers pending activation.
GET {{gateway}}/suppliers?status=PendingActivation&limit=50
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Sofia activates it, which publishes SupplierChanged version 1.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Either role blocks an active supplier, with a reason; version 2.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/block
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Bank details reported as changed by phone; checking with the supplier." }

### Only a supplier approver lifts the block; version 3.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/unblock
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### Propose a second account; the first stays in force until this one is approved.
# @name proposeAgain
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/bank-accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "iban": "GB29 NWBK 6016 1331 9268 19",
  "bic": "NWBKGB2L",
  "accountHolder": "Acme Deutschland GmbH"
}

### Sofia turns it down with a reason; nothing is published and the first account stays in force.
POST {{gateway}}/suppliers/{{create.response.body.id}}/bank-accounts/{{proposeAgain.response.body.bankAccounts[0].id}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "The letter was not on company paper." }

### Suppliers with a proposal waiting, a page at a time; pass "next" from the response as after=.
GET {{gateway}}/suppliers?hasPendingBankAccount=true&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{approverLogin.response.body.access_token}}

### The OpenAPI document, which needs no token.
GET http://localhost:5300/openapi/suppliers.json
